Cross-project implementation contract: https://github.com/joshyorko/rcc/issues/118

#118 now defines the concrete RCC/Holotree v1 path consumed here:

- cryptographic Environment Artifact Manifest + Object Index layered over existing v12 catalogs/current Hololib bytes;
- explicit separation between legacy SipHash cache keys and remote trust identities;
- provider publication/acquisition with verified objects and atomic manifest commit;
- worker-local materialization, lease, Execution Handle, and GC semantics;
- per-build/per-artifact/per-materialization coordination rather than a fleet-wide Holotree lock;
- source-only autoreload reuse and generation-safe environment-changing reload;
- a first two-process vertical that does not require a new catalog format, zstd, packfiles, FUSE, OCI, a daemon, or Kubernetes.

Treat #118 as the engine-side authority and this issue as the Runtime adapter/

## Implementation split and RCC lineage — 2026-08-18

This issue remains the full Actions environment-substrate contract. The board now has a bounded first implementation and explicit RCC dependencies.

### Immediate Actions child

- #134 — replace current local Action Server path/activation caching with an RCC EnvironmentBackend lifecycle while preserving current v2 package authoring, autoreload, frozen binary operation, and the existing process pool.

#134 is intentionally local/collapsed. It proves the Runtime can keep Environment Artifact/materialization/lease identity authoritative before #90 introduces independent workers.

